usage: rdap [-h]
            {try,doctor,health,selftest,init,raven-bind,identity,seal-under-session,relay-setup,trust,start,model,ask,ping,invite,discover,replies,goal,say,chat,status,watch,do,ls,board,mesh-build}
            ...

RDAP — signed agent-to-agent tasks. Newcomer path: `./rdap try` then `./rdap
init --name you --no-internet`. NON-RELEASE / HOLD active.

positional arguments:
  {try,doctor,health,selftest,init,raven-bind,identity,seal-under-session,relay-setup,trust,start,model,ask,ping,invite,discover,replies,goal,say,chat,status,watch,do,ls,board,mesh-build}
    try                 newcomer path: doctor + signed localhost selftest
                        (same as CI)
    doctor              check Python, Git, deps, signed-by-default, port, and
                        /health
    health              GET /health on a running node
    selftest            run the signed localhost A2A selftest (same suite as
                        CI)
    init                first-time setup of this agent
    raven-bind          M1 bind public same-RVN1 from raven-node whoami (NON-
                        RELEASE / HOLD; not confidential)
    identity            public RVN1 identity (NON-RELEASE / HOLD; bind is M1
                        public import)
    seal-under-session  M2 submit app payload to raven-node SealUnderSession
                        IPC (plaintext-to-daemon only; NON-RELEASE / HOLD; not
                        O6 Proven)
    relay-setup         configure the shared Git remote used by offline relay
    trust               register a teammate's invite
    start               serve this agent
    model               choose this agent's brain (LLM)
    ask                 delegate a task to a teammate
    ping                check whether a teammate node is reachable
    invite              print your invite line (add --port for url)
    discover            find nearby agents on this LAN (mDNS)
    replies             collect offline answers from git relay
    goal                set THE unified mission for all agents
    say                 group chat: @agent task | @all broadcast
    chat                show the shared team thread
    status              one-glance dashboard
    watch               live dashboard of all agents (no input)
    do                  short delegation: do WORKER "text" | do all "text"
    ls                  list teammates + last activity
    board               show the shared task board
    mesh-build          build EXPERIMENTAL PLAINTEXT mailbox binary (disabled
                        by default)

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit

OPEN MODE (--open / TEAM_REQUIRE_SIGNED=0) is never the default. Do not add
those flags for a first run. NON-RELEASE / HOLD active: raven-bind / identity
bind import public RVN1 only and do not claim confidential / atsam_rvn1 send.
seal-under-session is plaintext-to-daemon only; not O6 Proven; no HOLD lift;
seal still requires a raven-node session.
